<title>PORTUGAL: PT eyes business in Brazil, Africa.</title>
<headline>PT eyes business in Brazil, Africa.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal Telecom is seeking business opportunities in Brazil, Africa and southern China, its president, Murteira Nabo, was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>&quot;Brazil will be our big bet for the next five to 10 years. Africa, the Maghreb and southern China are other (priority) markets,&quot; Nabo told Diario Economico in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;We are discussing with our partners business opportunities in Brazil,&quot; he added. &quot;We are more interested in the fixed networks that will be privatised in Brazil.&quot;</p>
<p>He said he hoped that international business would rise to 30 percent of PT's revenues from two to three percent now.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
